# source (repo-relative, forward slashes) | target (%VAR% expanded by PowerShell)
# Prefixed 00- because the profile dot-sources drop-ins alphabetically.
powershell/dotfiles.ps1|%USERPROFILE%/Documents/PowerShell/drop-ins/00-gui-dotfiles.ps1
#
# Cross-platform tool configs. These files are identical on both platforms and
# only the target path differs, which is why they live in tool-named directories
# rather than under linux/ or windows/. Starship and micro both read from
# ~/.config on Windows too, so the paths happen to match the Linux map.
starship/starship.toml|%USERPROFILE%/.config/starship.toml
micro/settings.json|%USERPROFILE%/.config/micro/settings.json
#
# Claude Code config, shared with the Linux map. Directory sources, so a skill
# written in any session lands in this repo immediately.
ai/claude/CLAUDE.md|%USERPROFILE%/.claude/CLAUDE.md
ai/claude/skills|%USERPROFILE%/.claude/skills
ai/claude/commands|%USERPROFILE%/.claude/commands
#
# settings.json is per-platform, which is why it sits here and in linux/
# rather than in ai/claude/ with the files above. Claude Code reads exactly
# one user-level settings file, so there is no shared-core-plus-overlay to
# split it into: each platform needs its own complete copy. The Windows one
# carries statusLine and the notify hooks, which invoke pwsh scripts by
# absolute path; the Linux one omits both. Keep the rest of the two files in
# sync by hand -- they are short, and the alternative is a generator that
# breaks the symlink write-back the ai/claude/ entries above depend on.
windows/claude-settings.json|%USERPROFILE%/.claude/settings.json
#
# Historical note, kept because it cost a file: an earlier version of this map
# linked the repo's PROJECT context file (.claude/CLAUDE.md) over
# %USERPROFILE%\.claude\CLAUDE.md and destroyed the personal global instructions
# living there. They were always two different documents. The project one has
# since been folded into the root CLAUDE.md and deleted, and the global one now
# lives at ai/claude/CLAUDE.md — linked above, on both platforms.
